      "mergeID": "64122d9f2062230cab320880",
      "mergedPostDetails": "For a long time I've used a single Physbone component for multiple chains for my avatar's arm wings. I use the multi-child 'ignore' setting to \"mask\" out the IK bones by adding empty game objects to prevent them being effected by the Physbone.\n\nRecently (pretty sure build 1287) doing this now forces the IK bones with Physbones on them back into T-pose.\n\nThis causes my avatar's arms to be stuck straight while i can still move other bones (including shoulder bones) in game.\n\n(I'm not sure if this effects quest but it certainly effects PC-VR)",
      "mergedPostTitle": "Physbones on humanoid (IK) bones broken in build 1287",
      "parentID": null,
      "pinned": false,
      "postDeleted": false,
      "postID": "640b702c26e0a3454593f7c3",
      "private": false,
      "reactions": null,
      "sourceLink": null,
      "spam": false,
      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "I am having the same issue with my hair and chest bones while using the multi-child ignore setting, causing pretty much all of my avatars to not move properly from the chest up since the latest update.",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    },
